---
/**
 * Adds the funding acknowledgement to the foot of every docs page.
 *
 * Why it exists: the grant's Outputs Management Plan (section 7) requires
 * every output, the documentation site included, to carry the acknowledgement
 * word for word. Putting it in the footer reaches every Starlight page, the
 * splash home among them, without an edit to each page.
 *
 * Overriding `Footer` is Starlight's supported way in, the same as the
 * `SocialIcons` override beside the version chip. Rendering `<Default />` keeps
 * the edit link, last-updated date and pagination exactly as Starlight draws
 * them, through upgrades.
 *
 * The text must stay verbatim: src/__spec__/funding-acknowledgement.spec.ts
 * fails if it drifts here or anywhere else the acknowledgement appears. The
 * playground (src/pages/playground.astro) is not a Starlight page, so it does
 * not get this footer.
 */
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Footer.astro';
---

<Default />

<p class="pv-funding">
  This work was supported by the Research Software Maintenance Fund, managed by
  the Software Sustainability Institute and funded by UKRI grant reference
  AH/Z000114/1.
</p>

<style>
  @layer starlight.core {
    .pv-funding {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding-top: 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
      font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
      color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    }
  }
</style>
